  "assessmentTitle": "Give the model a starting point",
  "assessmentIntro": "Every number on the reading page comes either from your review history or from the model's defaults. This does a third thing: one short assessment that replaces the defaults with an estimate about you. It measures abstract parameters (starting retrievability, fluency), not how many cards you memorised; self-report starts, objective checks come later. Every prior is still marked uncalibrated - it is a starting point, not a conclusion.",
