  "assessmentStepSelf": "2. Self-report",
  "assessmentStepRecall": "3. Recall check",
  "assessmentStepResult": "4. Reading",
  "assessmentScopeHint": "Pick one area (a selected tag includes its children). The tighter the scope, the more the priors deserve to be taken seriously; spread over the whole library they are only an average.",
  "assessmentScopeCount": "{count} knowledge points in this area",
  "assessmentScopeEmpty": "Nothing to measure yet: create tags on the tags page and knowledge points in flashcards first.",
  "assessmentNext": "Next",
  "assessmentBack": "Back",
  "assessmentSkip": "Skip this time",
  "assessmentSelfHint": "Without looking anything up, how much could you retell right now? 0 = nothing at all, 5 = I could teach it. Self-report is not an exam; it gives the model a starting point, and objective checks will correct it.",
  "assessmentSelfAnswered": "Self-rated {answered} / {total}",
  "assessmentRecallHint": "These three knowledge points are the two ends and the middle of the scope - the same set every time, so different days can be compared. Write your retelling, then rate it: did it hold up?",
